t/issues/115333","id":3797001898,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iUaaq","user":{"login":"totoriel","id":132148700,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-Bt3A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132148700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel","html_url":"https://github.com/totoriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T17:40:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T17:40:28Z","body":"> This is not a bug, `make_current` isn't the same as `current = true`, nor does it say that it does\n\nWell, no, if we do look at the docs, we can see :\n\nvoid make_current() \n\nMakes this camera the current camera for the Viewport. If the camera node is outside the scene tree, it will attempt to become current once it's added. (Old logic most likely not up to date)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nbool current = false \n\nvoid set_current(value: bool)\nclass-bool is_current()\n\nIf true, the ancestor Viewport is currently using this camera.\n\nIf multiple cameras are in the scene, one will always be made current. For example, if two Camera3D nodes are present in the scene and only one is current, setting one camera's current to false will cause the other camera to be made current.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAlso, by looking at the code :\nvoid Camera3D::make_current() {\n\tcurrent = true;\n\n\tif (!is_inside_tree()) {\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\n\tget_viewport()->_camera_3d_set(this);\n}\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3797001898/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3797024962","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115333#issuecomment-3797024962","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115333","id":3797024962,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iUgDC","user":{"login":"DexterFstone","id":92402263,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYHyVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92402263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone","html_url":"https://github.com/DexterFstone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T18:02:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T18:02:53Z","body":"Both is the same because `set